    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-062 — `linear-gradient()` background support.** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCloses the last 1/11 `background:` form. **Synthetic-fixture verified only** — the Wikipedia gradient target is triple-blocked (pseudo-element, ancestor-culled parent, `position: sticky` deferred).\n\n## The verified delta (fixture, 2026-11-02)\n\n5-row fixture at `docs/adr062-gradient-test.html`:\n\n| Row | CSS | Render |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `background-color: #d35400` (control) | Solid orange ✓ |\n| 2 | `linear-gradient(red, blue)` (default 180deg) | **Vertical red→blue** ✓ |\n| 3 | `linear-gradient(45deg, red, blue)` | Diagonal ✓ |\n| 4 | `linear-gradient(to right, red, white, blue)` | Horizontal red→white→blue ✓ |\n| 5 | `linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0), white)` | Gray→white (Wikipedia form) ✓ |\n\n**All 5 render correctly.** Screenshot proof of gradient parsing + layout + Cairo pattern painting end-to-end.\n\n## The critical angle fix\n\nFirst implementation used math convention (`cos θ, sin θ` for direction). Rendered **horizontal instead of vertical** for the default 180deg case — because CSS linear-gradient angles are measured from \"up\" clockwise, in screen coordinates (y down).\n\n**Correct formula** (CSS Images 3 §3.1.1):\n- Direction vector: `(sin θ, -cos θ)` in screen coords\n- Gradient line length: `L = W·|sin θ| + H·|cos θ|`\n\n| CSS angle | Direction | Formula result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0° | up | (0, -1) → bottom→top |\n| 90° | right | (1, 0) → left→right |\n| 180° | down | (0, 1) → top→bottom ✓ default |\n| 270° | left | (-1, 0) → right→left |\n\nPre-fix, all angles rendered rotated 90°. Post-fix, all 4 conventions map correctly.\n\n## The unplanned prerequisite\n\n**`parse_color` had no `rgb()` / `rgba()` support.** Wikipedia's gradient starts with `rgba(255,255,255,0)` — without rgba parsing, the first stop silently fails, leaving 1 stop, no gradient paint.\n\n**Extended `parse_color`** (~50 lines): `rgb(r, g, b)` / `rgba(r, g, b, a)` with integer (0-255), percentage (0-100%), and mixed channel forms. Uses existing `split_commas` + `trim_ws`.\n\n**This is the same pattern as ADR-060's `#include` discovery** — a prerequisite the spec assumed existed but didn't. Recorded in the commit message as an honest finding.\n\n## What ships\n\n### Parser (`stylesheet.cpp`)\n\nReplaces blanket `if (gradient( in value) return false;` with targeted `linear-gradient(...)` extraction. Preserves raw gradient as `background-image: linear-gradient(...)`. Stray commas outside the gradient still drop (multi-layer). Radial/conic/repeating still drop.\n\n### `parse_color` (`style_values.cpp`)\n\n`rgb()` / `rgba()` support added. Integer (0-255), percentage (0-100%), mixed. `std::clamp` bounds. `std::stof` try/catch.\n\n### Data model (`layout_box.hpp`)\n\n```cpp\nstruct BackgroundGradientStop {\n    Color color;\n    float position;  // 0.0 .. 1.0\n};\nbool background_is_gradient = false;\nfloat background_gradient_angle_deg = 180.0f;\nstd::vector<BackgroundGradientStop> background_gradient_stops;\n```\n\n### Layout (`layout.cpp`)\n\n`parse_background_gradient` helper + local `gradient_detail` namespace. Splits on top-level commas, parses optional direction (`Ndeg` or `to <keyword>` incl. corners), then stop colors via `parse_color`. Positions parsed but ignored in v1 (uniform interpolation).\n\n**Note**: `split_commas` / `trim_ws` live in `style_values.cpp`'s anonymous namespace — duplicated locally in `layout.cpp` (`gradient_detail::g_split_commas`, `g_split_whitespace`, `g_trim`). Same pattern as ADR-056's `is_color_token` duplication.\n\n### Paint (`paint.cpp`)\n\n`paint_background_gradient`: CSS §3.1.1 half-diagonal formula, Cairo linear pattern with per-stop `add_color_stop_rgba`. Called in `paint_box` before `background_image_url` (gradient is fill, URL image layers on top).\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Zero Wikipedia delta.** Target triple-blocked.\n- **Stop positions** (`red 20%`) parsed but uniform interpolation applied.\n- **Radial / conic / repeating** dropped.\n- **Multi-layer** dropped.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 683 → 687 cases (+4 new)\n- 2614 → 2627 assertions (+13)\n- 1 test flipped (ADR-055's \"gradient dropped\" → \"preserved as background-image\")\n- Zero regression on 683 pre-existing tests\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Stop positions (uniform interpolation applied)\n- Radial / conic / repeating gradients\n- Multi-layer gradients\n- Color interpolation spaces (`in oklab`)\n- `position: sticky` (the target's third blocker)\n- Ancestor culling unblock (the target's second blocker)\n\nRefs #265\n",
